   "text": {
    "L1": "Read the situation before choosing an operation.",
    "L2": "A part of something means multiply. How many fit or equal sharing means divide.",
    "L3": "Put together means add, while taken away or left means subtract.",
    "L4": "A later fraction is often taken from what remains, not from the original amount.",
    "L5": "For example, one third of ₹600 is ₹200, so ₹400 remains.",
    "L6": "One fourth of the remaining ₹400 is ₹100, leaving ₹300.",
    "L7": "Use a bar model to show the whole and its parts, then check the answer's size and unit.",
    "L8": "Now choose the operation for each situation."
   },
